# SD:/etc/session/pocket -- the pocket session's programs: run by /bin/session (the autostart's line
# `session`) when SD:/etc/system.ini says "shell = pocket" (PocketUI, one app at a time on a small screen),
# ended when the mode is switched to another (the Control Panel's Mode, `session switch`). The same syntax
# as SD:/etc/autostart.
#
# The menu bar is always there: the front app's menus, the clock, the status icons (PocketUI takes it as its
# top band). No dock, no agenda, no Stickies in pocket.
run menubar
# The rest of the pocket shell -- the launcher, the switcher -- comes with PocketUI's phase P5
# (docs/POCKETUI-TECH-STUDY.md); it will be this file's line:
#   run pocketshell
# Until then the Terminal stands in for the launcher (`run <app>`, `session switch desktop`); Alt+Tab goes from
# one app to the next. The notifications: notifyd starts with the first one (SystemKit's notify) until
# pocketshell serves them (P5).
run terminal
